---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const title = "Relicta — Governed software releases";
const description = "Plan software releases, review risk, prepare release notes, apply approval policy, and keep an auditable decision record.";
---
<SiteLayout {title} {description}>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">Release planning, review, and governance</p>
      <h1>Turn software changes into reviewed releases.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Relicta analyzes repository changes, recommends a version, prepares release notes, applies your approval policy, and records the decision. People and AI agents can use the same release workflow.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn solid" href="https://docs.relicta.tech/install">Get started with the CLI</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/vision">Read the vision</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-card">
      <div class="terminal">
        <div class="abstract-diagram">
          <div class="diagram-node">Agent / CI</div>
          <div class="diagram-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="diagram-node node-relicta">Relicta</div>
          <div class="diagram-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="diagram-node">Production</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-foot">The decision layer for modern software delivery.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Numbers Bar -->
  <section class="numbers-bar reveal">
    <div class="number-item">
      <span class="number-value">8</span>
      <span class="number-label">Potential release-risk factors</span>
    </div>
    <div class="number-item">
      <span class="number-value">5</span>
      <span class="number-label">AI provider integrations</span>
    </div>
    <div class="number-item">
      <span class="number-value">4</span>
      <span class="number-label">Release-note audiences</span>
    </div>
    <div class="number-item">
      <span class="number-value">1</span>
      <span class="number-label">Recorded release decision</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Problem -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Problem</p>
      <h2>Software delivery scaled. Decision-making didn't.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Code is cheap. Changes are frequent. Risk is hidden. Trust erodes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Past</h3>
        <p>Human-written code. Human reviews. Human pace.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Now</h3>
        <p>Agent-generated change. CI automation. Overwhelmed humans.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-featured">
        <h3>The Gap</h3>
        <p>Governance. How do we trust the machine to ship?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What Relicta Is -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="grid">
      <div>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">The Solution</p>
          <h2>Relicta governs release decisions.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">Relicta analyzes repository changes, recommends a version, prepares release notes, applies configured policy, records approvals, and runs configured publishing steps.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div>
          <h4>The Core Decisions</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>What changed? (Semantic Analysis)</li>
            <li>Is it risky? (Risk Scoring)</li>
            <li>Who approves? (Governance)</li>
            <li>How to tell users? (Communication)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">How It Works</p>
      <h2>From commit to production, governed.</h2>
      <p class="lede">A reviewable workflow from repository changes to a published release.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">1</div>
        <h4>Plan</h4>
        <p>Analyze commits, detect breaking changes, calculate risk score, suggest version.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-connector"></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">2</div>
        <h4>Bump</h4>
        <p>Apply the proposed version to configured files. This step does not create a Git tag.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-connector"></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">3</div>
        <h4>Notes</h4>
        <p>Create release notes with deterministic templates or a configured AI provider. Agent-session customer notes are in the unreleased v5 source, not the current public release.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-connector"></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">4</div>
        <h4>Approve</h4>
        <p>Evaluate configured policy, collect required approvals, and record the decision in the audit trail.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-connector"></div>
      <div class="pipeline-step step-accent">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">5</div>
        <h4>Publish</h4>
        <p>Create the Git tag and run configured publisher integrations. Signing and provenance depend on the release workflow.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="terminal pipeline-terminal">
      <pre><code><span class="t-muted">$</span> relicta release

<span class="t-step">plan</span>    47 commits since v1.3.0 &middot; 2 breaking, 8 features, 12 fixes
        Risk: <span class="t-warn">0.58</span> (medium) &middot; Blast radius: 3/7 packages
        Suggesting: <span class="t-accent">v2.0.0</span> (major)

<span class="t-step">bump</span>    Version set to v2.0.0

<span class="t-step">notes</span>   Draft prepared for review
        Audience: public (one audience per draft)

<span class="t-step">approve</span> Policy: risk above configured threshold requires review
        Approved by: release owner
        Audit: SHA-256 hash chain entry recorded

<span class="t-step">publish</span> <span class="t-accent">&check;</span> GitHub release created
        <span class="t-accent">&check;</span> npm package published
        <span class="t-accent">&check;</span> Slack #releases notified
        <span class="t-accent">&check;</span> Release workflow evidence recorded

<span class="t-accent">Done.</span> v2.0.0 released with its configured decision record.</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="section-note">Illustrative workflow only. Exact output, approvals, publishers, and signing depend on the Relicta version and your configuration.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Relicta Capabilities -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Release governance</p>
      <h2>One workflow for release decisions and delivery.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Relicta brings version planning, risk signals, review, release communication, and decision records into a single workflow.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="diff-grid">
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">01</div>
        <h3>Change Governance Protocol</h3>
        <p>An open, vendor-neutral protocol specification for representing change-governance decisions across actors and transports.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">02</div>
        <h3>MCP-Native AI Agents</h3>
        <p>An MCP server lets compatible agents inspect plans, assess risk, and request release actions through configured governance checks. Agent-session customer-note drafting is in the unreleased v5 source.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">03</div>
        <h3>Configured risk signals</h3>
        <p>Scores reflect configured factors and available change evidence. Automatic outcome calibration is roadmap work, not a v4.2.0 feature.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">04</div>
        <h3>Blast Radius Analysis</h3>
        <p>Maps changed files to impacted packages, builds dependency graphs, and quantifies change scope before you release.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">05</div>
        <h3>Audience-Specific Narratives</h3>
        <p>Prepare summaries for engineering, product, executive, and customer audiences with configured communication workflows. Review generated or agent-authored text before approval; Relicta does not fact-check prose.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">06</div>
        <h3>Policy DSL</h3>
        <p>Composable governance rules support AND, OR, and NOT conditions. Define approval gates, team routing, and auto-approval criteria as code.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">07</div>
        <h3>Outcome calibration (roadmap)</h3>
        <p>v4.2.0 does not automatically learn risk weights from release outcomes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="diff-card">
        <div class="diff-number">08</div>
        <h3>Governance attestations</h3>
        <p>Record release decision context. Build provenance and artifact signing are separate and depend on the release workflow.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Product fit -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Where Relicta fits</p>
      <h2>Release automation with reviewable governance.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Relicta combines release planning and publishing with risk signals, configurable approval policies, and decision records.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trust & Security -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Trust & Security</p>
      <h2>Run releases in your environment, with controls you can inspect.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="trust-grid">
      <div class="trust-item">
        <h4>Run locally or in CI</h4>
        <p>The core workflow runs in your repository or CI environment. If you configure a hosted AI provider or external plugin, the data required by that provider or integration is sent to that service.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-item">
        <h4>Verifiable decision records</h4>
        <p>Release decisions can be recorded in a SHA-256 hash chain and checked with Relicta's audit verification command. The chain is tamper-evident; it does not prevent changes to the repository or storage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-item">
        <h4>Governance attestations</h4>
        <p>Governance attestations record release decision context. Build provenance and artifact signing are separate and depend on the release workflow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-item">
        <h4>Plugin trust is explicit</h4>
        <p>Plugins are unsigned and run as separate processes. Review plugins before enabling them; sandbox enforcement varies by platform and is not a complete security boundary.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-item">
        <h4>Software bills of materials</h4>
        <p>Release archives include SBOMs where published. They support software inventory and do not establish compliance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-item">
        <h4>Optional output redaction</h4>
        <p>The <code>--redact</code> option masks detected secrets and API keys in Relicta output and is automatically enabled in CI mode. It does not replace secure logging and secret-handling practices.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Available Release -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Available release: v4.2.0</p>
      <h2>Start with a release workflow you can review.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Relicta is open-source software. Review the current release notes, install guidance, and support limits before adopting it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="feature-list">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Semantic version planning</strong> from conventional commits — with heuristic fallback for messy histories</li>
          <li><strong>AI-assisted release notes</strong> via OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Azure, or Ollama</li>
          <li><strong>Approval & audit trail</strong> with configurable policy DSL</li>
          <li><strong>Plugin-based publishing</strong> — GitHub, npm, Docker, and Slack plugins, with additional registry entries whose verification status varies</li>
          <li><strong>MCP server</strong> — compatible agents can use release tools through configured policy gates</li>
          <li><strong>File, SQLite, and PostgreSQL state</strong> — choose a persistence mode that fits your deployment</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="hero-actions">
           <a class="btn solid" href="https://docs.relicta.tech/install">Install Relicta</a>
           <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/relicta-tech/relicta">View GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal">
        <img src="/demos/marketing.gif" alt="Relicta CLI usage" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- From Today -> Vision -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Evolution</p>
      <h2>From release automation to change governance</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="comparison-table">
      <div class="table-header">
        <div>Today</div>
        <div>Where It's Going</div>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <div>Version bumps</div>
        <div>Risk-aware decisions</div>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <div>Changelogs</div>
        <div>Outcome-based communication</div>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <div>CI automation</div>
        <div>Agent governance</div>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <div>Plugins</div>
        <div>Protocol ecosystem (MCP, CGP)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <div>Single repo</div>
        <div>Multi-repo federation</div>
      </div>
      <div class="table-row">
        <div>Pass/fail gates</div>
        <div>Probabilistic risk scoring</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who Relicta Is For -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Built For</p>
      <h2>Teams shipping from Git</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-cards">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Platform Engineers</h3>
        <p>Standardize configured release workflows across repositories. The current release supports a single project version; broader monorepo versioning strategies remain under evaluation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Release Managers</h3>
        <p>Review release risk, policy decisions, and approval status through the CLI workflow. The published v4.2.0 binaries do not include the dashboard; build from source to use it. Risk-based auto-approval follows your configured policies and does not replace review of high-risk or breaking changes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Security & Compliance</h3>
        <p>Review hash-chained governance audit records, release attestations, and SBOMs in published archives. Dashboard OIDC sign-in and role mapping are in the unreleased v5 source. Build provenance and artifact signing are separate release-workflow controls.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Teams Adopting Agents</h3>
        <p>Compatible agents can use Relicta's MCP release workflow to request plans and governed release actions. Relicta governs actions routed through that workflow; it does not control other tools the agent can access.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MCP / AI Agents -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">AI-Native</p>
      <h2>Use release tools from an MCP-compatible agent.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Relicta v4.2.0 provides an MCP server for release planning and governance. Agent-session customer-note drafting and interactive MCP Apps are in the unreleased v5 source.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mcp-demo">
      <div class="mcp-conversation">
        <div class="mcp-message user">
          <span class="mcp-label">You</span>
          <p>"What's the release risk for this project?"</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-message agent">
          <span class="mcp-label">Claude</span>
          <p>Risk score: 0.62 (medium). 3 breaking API changes detected across 2 packages. Blast radius: auth-service, api-gateway. Recommending v2.0.0 with 2-approver gate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-message user">
          <span class="mcp-label">You</span>
          <p>"Show me the release plan."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-message agent">
          <span class="mcp-label">Claude</span>
          <p>Relicta prepared a release plan. Approval and publication still require the configured governance and publisher steps.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="section-note">Illustrative conversation. Risk findings, version recommendations, and required approvals depend on the repository and configured policy.</p>
    <div class="mcp-tools-grid">
      <div class="mcp-tools-col">
        <h4>Tools (Agent Actions)</h4>
        <ul class="mcp-tool-list">
          <li><code>relicta_plan</code> Analyze commits & suggest version</li>
          <li><code>relicta_bump</code> Apply semantic version</li>
          <li><code>relicta_notes</code> Generate release notes</li>
          <li><code>relicta_evaluate</code> CGP risk evaluation</li>
          <li><code>relicta_approve</code> Governance gate</li>
          <li><code>relicta_publish</code> Execute release</li>
          <li><code>relicta_blast_radius</code> Impact analysis</li>
          <li><code>relicta_validate_release</code> Pre-flight checks</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="mcp-tools-col">
        <h4>Resources (Agent Reads)</h4>
        <ul class="mcp-tool-list">
          <li><code>relicta://state</code> Release state machine</li>
          <li><code>relicta://config</code> Project configuration</li>
          <li><code>relicta://commits</code> Pending commits</li>
          <li><code>relicta://changelog</code> Generated changelog</li>
          <li><code>relicta://risk-report</code> Risk assessment</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mcp-apps">
      <h3 class="mcp-apps-heading">MCP Apps in development for v5</h3>
      <p>These interactive apps are part of the unreleased v5 source and are not included in the current public v4.2.0 release.</p>
      <div class="mcp-apps-grid">
        <div class="mcp-app-card">
          <span class="mcp-app-icon">📊</span>
          <strong>Status Dashboard</strong>
          <p>Live release status at a glance</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-app-card">
          <span class="mcp-app-icon">🚀</span>
          <strong>Release Pipeline</strong>
          <p>Step-by-step release progress</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-app-card">
          <span class="mcp-app-icon">⚠️</span>
          <strong>Risk Assessment</strong>
          <p>Visual risk scoring breakdown</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-app-card">
          <span class="mcp-app-icon">🔍</span>
          <strong>Commit Review</strong>
          <p>Classified commit analysis</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-app-card">
          <span class="mcp-app-icon">✅</span>
          <strong>Approval Workflow</strong>
          <p>Interactive governance gates</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp-app-card">
          <span class="mcp-app-icon">💥</span>
          <strong>Blast Radius</strong>
          <p>Impact analysis across packages</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: 24px;">
      <a class="btn solid" href="https://docs.relicta.tech/mcp">MCP Integration Guide</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Open & Extensible -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open Source</p>
      <h2>Open by design. Extensible by default.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div>
        <p class="lede">We believe the governance layer must be open. No vendor lock-in. Full transparency.</p>
        <div class="feature-list">
            <ul>
                <li>Open CLI (MIT Licensed)</li>
                <li>gRPC plugin system; review plugin trust and platform sandbox status before enabling plugins</li>
                <li>MCP server for compatible agents; interactive app concepts are in the unreleased v5 source</li>
                <li>Change Governance Protocol specification</li>
                <li>Protocol-first mindset</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band reveal-scale">
    <div>
      <h2>Start governing change today.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Install the current release using the platform-specific steps in the documentation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn solid" href="https://docs.relicta.tech/install">Get started</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://docs.relicta.tech">Read the docs</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/vision">Follow the vision</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</SiteLayout>

<style>
  /* Hero diagram */
  .abstract-diagram {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 40px;
    color: var(--color-terminal-text);
  }
  .diagram-node {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 12px 24px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
  }
  .node-relicta {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: bold;
    box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(92, 240, 200, 0.2);
  }
  .diagram-arrow {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  /* Numbers Bar */
  .numbers-bar {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--color-border);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 32px 0;
  }
  .number-item {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 24px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .number-value {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .number-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  /* Pipeline */
  .pipeline {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 32px 0 24px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .pipeline-step {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 140px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 16px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .pipeline-step h4 {
    margin: 8px 0 4px;
  }
  .pipeline-step p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .pipeline-icon {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .step-accent .pipeline-icon {
    background: rgba(92, 240, 200, 0.15);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .pipeline-connector {
    width: 24px;
    min-width: 24px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--color-border);
    align-self: center;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .pipeline-terminal {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .pipeline-terminal pre {
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .pipeline-terminal code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .t-muted { color: #5a6a7a; }
  .t-step { color: #6b8afd; font-weight: 700; }
  .t-accent { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .t-warn { color: var(--color-accent-warm); }

  /* Differentiators Grid */
  .diff-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .diff-card {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 24px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .diff-card:hover {
    border-color: rgba(92, 240, 200, 0.3);
  }
  .diff-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
